# Fishing admin abuse events

When the user asks to run a **global** Fishing Idle event — phrases like `2x luck admin abuse`, `5x sell 10m admin abuse`, `3x money 15 minutes`, or similar — do this immediately (do not only explain how):

## Preferred (instant): MantleDB POST

```powershell
$now = [DateTimeOffset]::UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()
$mins = 5          # from user, clamp 1–180
$mult = 2          # from user, clamp 1.5–100
$until = $now + ($mins * 60 * 1000)
$body = @{
  token = "ice-fish-evt-9f3a"
  kind = "money"   # or "luck"
  until = $until
  startedAt = $now
  mult = $mult
  note = "admin-abuse"
} | ConvertTo-Json -Compress
Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri "https://mantledb.sh/v2/icedragon1st-mygames/fishing-admin-events" -ContentType "application/json" -Body $body
```

Clear early: set `until = 0`.

## Fallback: Pages JSON

If Mantle fails, write `fishing/admin-event.json` with `kind`, `until`, `startedAt`, `mult` (no token) and commit + push.

Defaults: **2×** for **5 minutes** unless the user specifies otherwise.

ICE_DRAGON can also use the in-game **Admin** button (mult + minutes fields, or commands like `5x sell 10m`).

Scheduled :00/:30 events still run; an active admin override replaces them until `until`.
